<http://data.silknow.org/object/f224f8d0-f144-3c95-83d9-78e9ef90d79c/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Piece, irregular rectangle, made of two pieces sewn together. Dark blue pattern on natural ground. Two wide stripes defined by white fretwork and delicate flowering vine against blue; between these, a vertically repeated unit showing a four-light stone Gothic window between clusters of lilies, roses and other flowers, ivy and a butterfly. Right-hand piece browned and slightly faded; light brown stains on both pieces. A few small holes."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f224f8d0-f144-3c95-83d9-78e9ef90d79c> .

